  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The way avatar pedestals work is by \"renting\" an avatar from the pedestal until you change and you have to go back to the world you originally got it from\n\nA lot of people want the ability to save these avatars rather than finding/creating one and uploading to unity\n\nA solution to this is to create a new feature called \"save slots\" the way it will work is that the player can save a rented avatar to a \"world slot\" by do you want to slot this avatar?\"  and be able to keep it until it is replaced by a new slotted avatar \n\nBut then the question is \"what if I want more than one save slot?\"\nHere's the answer: player choice\n\nLet us set up a possible example of what could be used to gain save slots: \"Bits\", player rank, and achievements\n\nA Good portion of the Vrchat community has been asking for a \"bits\" system or a  ranking system for the game, the idea is that the player is rewarded for playing the game or beating a developer choice map\n\nThe idea is that rewarding players for their dedication to not just playing, but talking and chatting with people, with the new rating system coming to the game, it opens up new opportunities for players and map creators alike to EARN slots\n\nThis is only an example but I believe we could come up with a optimal method to do this but it comes down to community choice whether we can implement this a system that can do this or just make a maximum of save slots",
